# Docker does not read .gitignore. Everything gitignored that matters is
# repeated here, because the failure mode is a credential store baked into an
# image layer and pushed to a registry.
#
# Deliberately no `!negation` patterns. The Dockerfile needs notebooks/config.py
# and data/reference.db, and a re-include that silently loses to a later rule
# breaks the build in a way that reads as a missing file rather than a bad
# ignore rule. Exclusions here are specific instead.

# --- never, under any circumstances ---
.env
.env.*
data/runtime/
data/device_tokens.json
data/device_tokens.json.migrated
data/fantasy_data.db
*.pem
*.key

# --- not reachable from a request ---
# The image runs src/ plus notebooks/config.py. Everything else in notebooks/ is
# a script or a notebook that only ever runs locally.
notebooks/*.ipynb
notebooks/build_reference_db.py
notebooks/compute_availability.py
notebooks/compute_league_bias.py
notebooks/create_indexes.py
notebooks/export_draft_fixture.py
notebooks/pull_projections.py
notebooks/rebuild_projections.py
notebooks/utils.py
tests/
docs/
draft-board/
figures/

# --- build and tooling noise ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
requirements.txt
